<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Retrieves the corresponding graph from a group of graphs :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`
:raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

.. note::
   ``nullptr`` is the &quot;not found&quot; answer, following
   :cpp:func:`IniSectionGraph::getSection`&apos;s found-or-``nullptr``-or-throw
   convention
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>graphGroups</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The group of graphs for each .ini file </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>id</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Which graph to retrieve </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>errorOnNotFound</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Whether to throw when no graph is found. <bold>Default</bold>: <computeroutput>true</computeroutput></para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::out_of_range</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>If no graph is found and &apos;errorOnNotFound&apos; is <computeroutput>true</computeroutput></para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><verbatim>embed:rst 
The found graph, or ``nullptr`` if there is none and &apos;errorOnNotFound&apos; is ``false``.
Non-owning -- the graph stays owned by &apos;graphGroups&apos;
</verbatim> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
